pick.verdict_on_current_design:
RESTRUCTURE, not keep and not rebuild.

The node inventory is mostly right, and much of the code is good and reused unchanged:
- the gateway and ledger;
- T8 contract + Jev ranking + human pick;
- choose_keyword;
- sentence-level, source-cited repair with splice_checked (fixes F9 about 49% of the time vs 0/6 for a full rewrite);
- step_guard / repair_contract;
- the deterministic finalizers;
- the degraded registry and _degraded_final;
- the publish gate;
- the citation tags;
- Q0 CI.

The WIRING is unsound in five ways that no amount of patching fixes:
(1) There is no single policy source. Source fidelity is restated in about 10 places, with 16 contradictions (3 meta bands, 6 background widths, CTA overwritten by ensure_cta, faq_filter KEEP vs drop_unanswerable_faq).
(2) There is no single fact source. Writer, F9 and eval judge each see a different, silently budgeted version of LLM-written prose (facts.py:40-76; the eval judge cuts 16000/9000).
(3) A hold-capable LLM judge works without an instrument record. F9 decides 34/99 holds, is uncalibrated and unpinned, and has been answered 72/72 by its third rung since 05/11. Judge fallbacks go unmarked: _note_fallback_write returns for any role other than writer, client.py:864-868 (VERIFIED). No raw reply is stored. F9PassMemory and the AA-528 guard exist only to absorb this noise.
(4) Quality comes from verify-and-repair, not from generation: 4/187 blogs passed at attempt 1. The writer is never given the rules that block it, so every new failure became another gate or fixer, inside a 750-line function with ~9 routing sets.
(5) The gated text is not the shipped text. _cut_stock_lines, _enforce_authenticity, strip_citation_tags and t9_faq_answer_fit run after the last gate (service.py:2443-2481, VERIFIED). And the verdict has no product consequence: held -> 'ready' (service.py:2777) and published (v1_publish.py:291 and :411-416, VERIFIED, AA-770). So attempt 3 buys only an admin label.

Only two nodes are actually rebuilt: F9 becomes a pinned, calibrated claim verifier on a shared fact pack, and the loop control becomes a policy-generated route table with a stop rule. Everything else is re-wired (cheap checks before the paid write, edits before the final gate) or merged.

A full rebuild, such as a parallel v2 graph, is rejected: it doubles the maintenance surface while the evidence base is 1 human blog label and 6 live blogs since 19/10. The restructure is done in place, behind a cassette replay that proves zero undeclared diffs at each step.

The product consequence is redefined. Since tenants always receive content, the protection for the reader is that residual unsupported trip promises are CUT before delivery (generalised truth cut). "Held" becomes an honest label for non-truth residue.

