pick.verdict_on_current_design:
RESTRUCTURE, not rebuild.

The generator half is sound and should be reused as-is:
- the code-built verbatim fact sheet and the code-decided day plan (s1_writer_v2.py:79-106, 162-219);
- writer v2's restraint rules (panel: 0.0015 vs 0.051 serious errors per sentence);
- the forbidden strip and repair_contract;
- the grounding node pattern (per sentence, fail-closed numbers, sentence-only repair, re-check);
- the degraded hold and route_guard;
- the ledger.

The control half after the writer is unsound, and this is why fixes have looped for weeks.

(1) The only routing variable is a saturated lint mean that cannot fail. VERIFIED: should_retry routes on score alone (graph.py:1263-1272); avg 9.99 / p10 10.00 over n=814. So the hard codes that say "regenerate" never regenerate.

(2) The fact sheet is thrown away after the writer, so every verifier and repair re-derives its own source view. flag_fix sees none at all (flag_fix_node.py:605-621).

(3) Repairs rewrite whole fields without the source, and the detector that triggered a repair is never re-run. VERIFIED: graph.py:1397-1398, "we don't re-run it here — judge is the post-fix brand gate". That judge is report-only (judge_node.py:369).

(4) Six entries and exits apply different guard sets. VERIFIED: hitl -> END at graph.py:1497 skips grounding, final_day_guard, degraded hold and route_guard. Every new guard therefore misses the other paths.

(5) The gates that act (meal regex, elephant regex, meta blocks, Jev "enforce") have no measured precision or recall. The only measured checker suite, run_checks, is offline-only (VERIFIED: imported only by scripts/aa645 and scripts/s1_step01). The one LLM judge that runs is uncalibrated (kappa 0.03), unpinned and decides nothing.

(6) Policy lives in contradicting copies (4 meta bands), and route, effort and memory-release changes bypass any eval.

These are graph-topology problems, not prompt problems. More prompt or regex patches cannot converge them. The fix is to reshape the control plane around one persisted source object, one code contract used both mid-graph and at a single exit, local source-aware repair, and replay-gated change control. The writer stays put.

props.test_plan:
Tier 0, $0 (no LLM), must pass before any paid run.
(a) Q0 cases for each class, red on the base code: missing/merged day; number not in the source; number-noun mismatch; a name outside the source with a tenant-brand name allowed; inclusion contradicted; 'Inclusions: None' prompt render; meal/clock invented vs a source-backed meal line kept; meta cut/long/short; forbidden word reintroduced by a repair; an em-dash edit changing meta length after the check; 'elephant riding' in the itinerary (not highlights); hitl exit skipping the audit.
(b) A graph-shape test with a scripted fake LLM client proves that every path (clean, repair, rewrite, budget exhausted, judge error, writer fallback to gpt-6-luna-openai) passes through finalize -> verify -> select_best -> save. It also proves that writer calls stay <= 3 even when the job is retried, and that no voice score triggers a write.
(c) Replay corpus: about 40 stored T2 versions from the synthetic audit tenants, plus the AA-729 s1 fixture and the step-1 ground truth. Run t2_checks.run over the stored output with the stored source and report TPR/TNR per class (Wilson 95%). A class gates status only if its precision lower bound is >= 0.8; otherwise its severity is set to report in the registry. A tour_replay_r0 job reruns this on deploy and turns verify red on any hard-finding flip.
(d) Run the new verifier in SHADOW inside the current pipeline for one deploy. It writes the vector into generation_meta, so a base-vs-new comparison exists on the same versions.
Tier 1, cents. A pinned t2_judge v2 rejudge of the t2@2 golden set (refresh to >= 12 pairs, >= 3 pass / >= 3 fail labelled by the panel + tech lead) at about $0.002 per call, under $0.10 per run. The run aborts if trace_models shows another model. Pass is kappa >= 0.6; below that the judge stays report-only, and nothing else in the design depends on it. Also measure the Jev a1_claim_supported clear precision on T2 pairs from the stored grounding hits; it stays shadow if precision is unmeasured or low.
Tier 2, paid, small subsets on the synthetic tenants only. First 3 tours with the new graph (~$0.30) as a smoke test: 0 cuts (stop=max_tokens), judge served at route position 0, replay record complete. Then 20 tours A/B, base vs new and effort high vs medium (~$2-4 total).
Pass criteria on the 20:
- hard findings on saved versions = 0;
- fidelity findings per version <= 50% of base;
- 0 forbidden words, meta in band 100%;
- days preserved 100%;
- writer calls per version p95 <= 2 and max <= 3;
- cost per version p95 <= $0.15;
- elephant tours all labelled policy_hold, ride text unchanged;
- voice score (report) not worse than base by more than the judge's measured noise band;
- cross-tenant similarity to master reported, with no gate.
Total validation spend stays under $5.

props.migration_path:
P0 (days 1-2, $0, independent of the new graph):
- gateway same-model retry on an empty or max_tokens reply, with a fallback_writer mark;
- drop gpt-6-luna-openai from t2_generate and nova-lite from the T2 judge routes (with a break-glass reason recorded: removal of uncalibrated rungs);
- bind family_rule.trace_models in the T2 job;
- make t2_judge report-only for status. Status comes from T3 hard codes until N4 exists, and T3_FULL_REWRITE is set to off;
- fix the prompt manifest entry and hash the full rendered prompt;
- elephant POLICY_HOLD branch;
- remove the hitl END bypass (route it through brand_audit);
- stop replacing a zero score with the master score.

P1 (week 1, $0):
- label t2@2 with the agent panel; the tech lead approves disagreements;
- Q0 T2 cases;
- SourceBundle plus fact sheet;
- single verifier N4 built from s1_checks, T3 and brand_claims;
- replay record persistence;
- the R0 job and the nightly watchdog;
- fill calibration blocks from Stage A2.

P2 (week 1-2, $0):
- run N4 in SHADOW on every live T2 job and on the stored corpus, comparing its finding vector with today's T3 outcome;
- write the policy registry and render the repair and verifier prompts from it.

P3 (week 2, cents then ≤ $5):
- T2 v2 writer prompt, N5 repair, N6 scoped rewrite, N4b verifier (shadow), N8 voice (report-only), all behind stage config t2_graph=v2;
- run Stages B and C;
- ship v2 as the default only on a C2 pass, and record the eval_run_id on the route and stage config change.

P4 (after the pass):
- delete the nudge, t2_judge_tiebreak, T2 flag_fix, revise_block, the judge in revalidate, the T3 full-graph round and the ~10 T2 env flags;
- reuse the same registry and verifier for A1 (S1 v2 already has the fact table), so later A1 fixes reach T2 by design;
- writing-memory releases for T2 activate only on R2 pass against t2@2.

P5 (ongoing):
- promote N4b classes or the voice score to enforce or selection only when their R1 numbers clear the bar;
- relabel 10 new versions monthly, to measure drift and keep n_pos growing.

